/*
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
    UICharacterSheet.uss
    Character Sheet  —  Structure & Layout only
    Unity UIToolkit  (Unity 6.x LTS)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

    PURPOSE
    ───────
    All sizing, spacing, flex directions, and positioning
    for the character sheet. NO colors or fonts here —
    those are in FishMMO-Theme.uss.

    ONE sheet, TWO windows. UITKEquipment and UITKInspect
    mount the same tree and read the same rules; the only
    difference is the .sheet--inspect class UITKInspect adds
    at runtime, declared right below .eq-panel. The eq- prefix
    predates the sheet being shared and is kept because
    WindowOverlapTests pins the window by its eq-panel class —
    read it as "the sheet", not as "equipment only".

    LOAD ORDER in UXML (required):
        <ui:Style src="FishMMO-Theme.uss" />
        <ui:Style src="UICharacterSheet.uss" />

    Unity UIToolkit layout rules used throughout:
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    • flex-direction defaults to column — set row explicitly
      on every horizontal container.
    • flex-shrink: 0 on every fixed-size element so Unity's
      Yoga solver never compresses it.
    • Absolute-positioned children need all four inset
      values (left/top/right/bottom) to fill their parent.
    • Give every flex parent a concrete size on at least
      one axis so children can resolve their own sizes.
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
*/

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   PANEL ROOT
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/*
    Anchored explicitly. Each panel is its own UIDocument whose root fills the screen, so a
    root with a size but no position resolves to the top-left corner — with the uGUI layer
    gone, every one of these panels stacked there on top of each other. Dragging overwrites
    left/top, which is why position is absolute here.

    The character sheet, the bank and the bag can be open at the same time — the bank opens the
    bag itself — and they are siblings in ONE UI Toolkit panel, ordered by UIDocument.sortingOrder.
    A click on a socket that another window covers is delivered to that window instead, so the
    three are tiled across the panel's width rather than stacked in the corners they used to
    share. Issue #268: with the sheet against the right edge, the bag and the bank covered eight
    of its ten equipment sockets, so a bank item dragged onto a socket landed in the bag, moved
    there, and locked the slot it landed in.

        character sheet     12 ..  532      left: 1%,  520 wide
        bank               552 ..  882      left: 46%, 330 wide
        bag                908 .. 1188      right: 1%, 280 wide

    Panel space is always exactly 1200 units wide (PanelSettings matches width), so these
    percentages are a fixed horizontal arrangement at every aspect ratio. Any move here has to
    be matched in the other two stylesheets; WindowOverlapTests fails if the three stop being
    disjoint, or if any of them leaves the panel.
*/
.eq-panel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1%; top: 12%;
    width: 520px;
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-shrink: 0;

    /*
        The slot grid and the attribute list used to take turns on one tab, so the panel was
        only ever as tall as the taller of the two. Both are drawn together now, which is
        enough to run off the bottom of a short screen, so the panel is capped and .eq-footer
        below is the half that shrinks to fit.
    */
    max-height: 84%;
}

/*
    THE INSPECT VARIANT — placement only.

    A window showing somebody else's character is opened to be compared against your own, so it
    belongs in the middle of the screen where your sheet and theirs are both readable, not tiled
    against the right edge. It is centred by default and the player drags it wherever they want:
    UITKControl.CanDrag already defaults true and this tree's header is already name="panel-header",
    which is the resolved drag handle, so movability costs nothing here. Nothing about the position
    persists — it is per-open, and a visual-tree rebuild puts it back in the middle.

        1200 units  −  520 wide  =  680  →  680 / 2  =  340

    It CANNOT be disjoint from the sheet, the bank and the bag: those three already tile the whole
    1200-unit panel (see the note above .eq-panel) and a 520px window has nowhere left to go.
    Issue #268 established what that costs — a covered UI Toolkit window is deaf rather than
    hidden — so the inspect window covers part of the sheet's right column and part of the bank on
    purpose, and the player moves it. Narrowing this variant is the lever if that ever reads badly.

    WindowOverlapTests is unaffected by any of this. That fixture mounts the UXML bare, with no
    component and no OnStarting, so a class added at runtime is invisible to it and the authored
    .eq-panel placement above is the only one it ever lays out.
*/
.eq-panel.sheet--inspect {
    left: 340px;
    top: 12%;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   HEADER
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    height: 40px;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.eq-header__left {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    flex: 1;
}

.eq-header__icon {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: 8px;
}

.eq-header__title {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: 4px;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   BODY  (three-column row)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-body {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: stretch;
    height: 320px;
    padding: 12px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* ── Side columns ──────────────────────────────────────── */

.eq-col {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-around;
    width: 68px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

/* ── Center column ─────────────────────────────────────── */

.eq-center {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    flex: 1;
    margin-left: 6px;
    margin-right: 6px;
}

/* ── Character preview ─────────────────────────────────── */

.eq-preview {
    width: 100%;
    flex: 1;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    position: relative;
}

.eq-preview__rt {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

.eq-preview__label {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}

/* ── Center sub-slots row (Neck / Back / Ring) ─────────── */

.eq-center-slots {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    height: 64px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.eq-center-slots .eq-slot {
    margin-left: 4px;
    margin-right: 4px;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   EQUIPMENT SLOT
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-slot {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    position: relative;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

/* Icon: fills slot, leaves room at bottom for the label */
.eq-slot__icon {
    position: absolute;
    left: 5px;
    top: 5px;
    right: 5px;
    bottom: 14px;
}

/* Slot name label pinned to bottom.
   The names are written out in full (issue #257). Unity's default theme puts a box on every
   Label that nothing here contradicted: measured on these sockets it made the label 18px tall
   for a 10px line, which lifted the text to y 37..47 across an icon that ends at y 41, and its
   uneven side margins (2px / 4px) pulled the text 1.5px left of centre. Zeroing the box puts
   the line at y 43..53, below the icon, centred on the socket. Width was never the constraint:
   the longest name, "Main Hand", measures 41px against 54px. */
.eq-slot__label {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 2px;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 0;
    padding-right: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Stack count badge — bottom-right corner */
.eq-slot__amount {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 14px;
    right: 3px;
    padding-left: 2px;
    padding-right: 2px;
}

/* Cooldown: full-slot overlay */
.eq-slot__cooldown {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

/* Lock: full-slot overlay */
.eq-slot__lock {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
}

/*
    Waiting on the server, as opposed to locked by the container.
    Both mean "this slot is busy", so they share one overlay element and differ only in
    colour: a container lock is a refusal (danger tint, inherited from .fish-slot__lock),
    an in-flight request is just a wait. The override is a neutral scrim rather than a
    second danger tint so the player can tell a pending click from a rejected one.
*/
.eq-slot__lock--pending {
    background-color: var(--scrim-60);
    border-color: var(--brand-border);
    border-width: 1px;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   FOOTER  (attribute scroll list)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-footer {
    flex-direction: column;
    max-height: 200px;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;

    /*
        The one part of the panel allowed to lose height when .eq-panel hits its cap. Yoga will
        not shrink a flex child below its content unless min-height is cleared, so both are
        needed; the ScrollView inside absorbs the loss.
    */
    flex-shrink: 1;
    min-height: 0;
}

/* Sits directly under .eq-divider, which already carries the gap. */
.eq-attr-heading {
    margin-top: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.eq-divider {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.eq-attr-scroll {
    flex: 1;
}

/* ── Attribute rows (layout for runtime-generated elements) */

.fish-attr-category {
    margin-top: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
}

.fish-attr-row {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 3px;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
    padding-left: 2px;
    padding-right: 2px;
}

.fish-attr-row__name {
    flex: 1;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   STATUS BAR
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-status-bar {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    height: 28px;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 12px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}

.eq-chip {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-right: 12px;
}

.eq-chip__dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-right: 4px;
}

.eq-chip__label {
    margin-right: 3px;
}

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   UTILITY
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.eq-hidden { display: none; }
